# Windows dialogs (multiplayer wizard, save / load) keep the game colours.
# Before a dialog the game draws its screen with GDI through a 236-entry logical palette meant for
# entries 10..245 and realizes it on the game window. cnc-ddraw's RealizePalette copies that palette
# into DirectDraw entries 0..235, shifting every colour by 10 until the game loads another palette.
# The realize calls become "add esp, 4" (their one stdcall argument) so the DirectDraw palette, which
# already holds these colours, is left alone.
verify 414C9D 2e ff 15 d4 01 62 00
patch  414C9D 83 c4 04 90 90 90 90
verify 486576 2e ff 15 d4 01 62 00
patch  486576 83 c4 04 90 90 90 90
